{"id": "P00216", "name": "Edwin Chen", "name_chinese": "Edwin Chen", "country": "United States", "net_worth_usd_m": "18000.0", "net_worth_source": "Forbes real-time", "source_of_wealth": "Artificial intelligence", "industry": "technology", "sec_insider_companies": "", "shared_with": "", "appears_on": "Forbes real-time (2026); Hurun Global (2026); Hurun Global U40 (2026); Wikidata (2025)", "focus": ["data_center_ai"], "forbes_profile_url": "https://www.forbes.com/profile/edwin-chen/", "wikidata_url": "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q136480349", "forbes_bio": ["Edwin Chen is the CEO of Surge AI, which he founded in 2020 to help companies label data to train AI.", "Surge generated $1.2 billion in 2024 revenue from customers like Google and AI lab Anthropic.", "Notably, Surge claims it has not yet raised any outside funding; Chen owns an estimated 75% of the company.", "Before founding Surge, the Florida native worked for Twitter, Google, Facebook and Peter Thiel's hedge fund Clarium.", "Chen attended MIT, where he studied math, computer science and linguistics."], "forbes_facts": ["At MIT, Chen researched how to decode an Incan language expressed via knots tied in rope."]}
{"id": "P01338", "name": "N. Murray Edwards", "name_chinese": "N·默里·爱德华兹", "country": "Canada", "net_worth_usd_m": "5042.6", "net_worth_source": "Forbes real-time", "source_of_wealth": "Oil & gas", "industry": "energy", "sec_insider_companies": "", "shared_with": "", "appears_on": "Forbes real-time (2026); Forbes annual (2006-2025); Hurun Global (2014-2026)", "focus": ["energy"], "forbes_profile_url": "https://www.forbes.com/profile/n-murray-edwards/", "wikidata_url": "", "forbes_bio": ["N. Murray Edwards derives much of his fortune from stakes in Canadian oil and mining companies.", "His largest investments include oil sands miner Canadian Natural Resources, aerospace firm Magellan and a minority stake in the NHL's Calgary Flames.", "A lawyer by training, Edwards made the jump to business at age 28 after promising a dying friend that he would always pursue his passions.", "He started a merchant bank with partners in the late 1980's, but they spent half their initial capital on digging a natural gas well that came up dry.", "Edwards then switched gears and diversified from exploration to investing in existing oil and gas assets."], "forbes_facts": ["Edwards worked four nights a week during high school as a hockey referee.", "The Saskatchewan native also worked as a garbage crew member and once had a summer job at a beer factory that gave him unlimited beer during his breaks."]}
